# not from a tape — written for the app, so there is no v1 line to match.
@segment  remote-viewing-intent
@title    Setting the Target
@levels   F10
@duration ~55s
@upright
@needs    paper, something to write with
@fixed

# Done sitting up, before anything else, while the listener is still fully
# awake and can hold a pen.
#
# The tape never had this step -- it assumes you already know what you are
# reaching for. Written down beforehand, the target stops being something to
# hold in mind during the exercise, which is the thing that pulls you out of
# it. The paper also outlasts the session, which is the point: what you wrote
# before is what you check against afterwards.
#
# @fixed: this is an instruction, and an instruction that rephrases itself is
# an instruction you have to read twice.

say Before we begin, sit up for a moment. You will need something to write on.
pause 6
say Write down what you intend to look for. A person, a place, an object, a moment in time. One line is enough.
pause 10
say Be as specific as you are willing to be. If you only have a question, write the question.
pause 8
say Now put it somewhere you can reach when this is over, face down, and leave it there.
pause 6
say That is the last thing you have to do awake. Lie down, and make yourself comfortable.
pause 8
